id: pm-j8spis
title: Resume due telemetry after a concurrent background upload
description: "A real source get finish remained queued for432.545 seconds until a later invocation, though it eventually paired. The detached worker flushes one snapshot; a concurrent completion can append after that snapshot while its foreground scheduling is refused by the active flush lock. Reconcile and schedule due tail work after releasing that lock, without foreground network I/O, busy retries, or recreating removed storage."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[3]: delivery,sdk,telemetry
created_at: "2026-10-13T16:48:11.966Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-13T18:58:50.981Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-13T17:53:26.144Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-13T17:53:26.144Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: A deterministic real-SDK worker collector receives a finish appended during the first POST without a subsequent user command; future-backoff work does not spin; disabled consent or removed storage cannot restart workers; event and OTLP tail work are covered; existing SDK/CLI performance and security gates pass.
parent: pm-5oj5
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Detached SDK workers continue due event and span draining after releasing each upload lock, rechecking consent and identity and stopping on unchanged work or future retry backoff"
expected_result: A completion appended during an upload reaches the collector without another user command and without foreground network work
actual_result: "The real-worker control times out before correction and passes after correction;156 linked telemetry tests cover consent, removed storage, stagnant work and future OTLP retries; typecheck, lint, secrets, SDK/graph/record/mutation and9 packed consumers pass, while exact hosted coverage and static remain mandatory before merge"
